What this project does
It builds and evaluates a fraud-detection pipeline using transaction data, then predicts fraud probability for new records.

Main files
app.py

Main fraud pipeline
Loads CSV data
Performs preprocessing and feature engineering
Optionally balances the training set with SMOTE-style methods
Trains an XGBoost fraud classifier
Optionally tunes hyperparameters with Optuna
Optionally calibrates predicted probabilities
Evaluates performance using metrics like PR-AUC, ROC-AUC, precision, and recall
Produces a trained model and can run predictions
fraud_client.py

Client wrapper around app.py functionality
Loads train.csv, trains the model, then loads test.csv
Runs line-by-line probability prediction for each test record
Saves output to predictions.csv
train_data.py

Synthetic data generation helper
Creates a fake transaction dataset with customer, merchant, location, amount, device, and fraud label fields
Writes train.csv (and can be adapted for additional data)
Core feature engineering in app.py
The pipeline creates many fraud-relevant derived features, including:

Date/time features from trans_date and trans_time
Cyclical encodings for hour/month/day of week
Merchant risk features based on merch_id
Customer transaction behavior and velocity features from amt
Geographic distance features using lat, long, merch_lat, merch_long
Amount transformations and high/low/round amount flags
Age features from dob
Label encoding for categorical columns like gender, category, state, customer_device, customer_payment_method
What the project is for
Demonstrates a full fraud-detection workflow:
data loading
feature engineering
class balancing
model training
evaluation
prediction export
Uses XGBoost as the model backend
Provides a command-line client to generate per-record fraud probabilities
